WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 3 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:07.749
A colleague discovers a different error in fictional TS-088, which has already been invoiced.

00:00:07.989 --> 00:00:12.405
The ordinary submitted-sheet correction path is no longer the right assumption.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:22.011
SAP documents a revised-time-sheet process for eligible cases; configuration and the worker or supplier’s role affect who can perform it.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:33.175
Your supervisor task is to preserve a clear handoff: record identifier, affected date and line, original value, verified proposed value, and source evidence.

00:00:33.415 --> 00:00:39.197
Ask the designated program office or supplier contact to use the approved revision process.

00:00:39.437 --> 00:00:44.941
Avoid creating a second ordinary time sheet for the same work merely to offset the error.

00:00:45.631 --> 00:00:53.119
Worked exception: TS-088 Friday DEL shows 8, supported record shows 6, status Invoiced.

00:00:53.359 --> 00:01:00.633
Handoff: ‘Please review the approved revision route for TS-088; Friday differs by 2 DEL hours.

00:01:00.873 --> 00:01:08.383
Source record attached in the authorized system.’ In this public sample, no attachment or real worker data is transmitted.

00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:13.745
Close the loop by checking that the responsible owner accepted the correction request.

00:01:13.985 --> 00:01:17.697
A submitted request is not a completed financial adjustment.

00:01:17.937 --> 00:01:24.955
The assessment now combines identification, reconciliation, decision quality, and truthful status reporting.

00:01:25.645 --> 00:01:26.733
Now it's your turn.

00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:29.683
TS-088 is already invoiced.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.459
Which response is safest?

00:01:31.699 --> 00:01:34.813
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

